mn dragon now  and that dragon already brought down the  magical wall so he may be capable of  just about anything  there will be an x factor though  Daenerys has two dragons of her own and  Melisandre should be showing up as well  and she could possibly be bringing her  own weapons of fire that can counteract  the knight Kings ice magic Melisandre  still has a massive role to play and  whatever it is will cause her death so  there is no telling what kind of demons  she could summon upon the army of the  Dead whatever it is it should be very  interest  to see more and more spoilers are  starting to come out and everything  that's taking place in the north is  getting me very excited unfortunately  for the Starks they may have to abandon  their ancestral home and flee from the  north I don't want to go too far down  that road right now though because there  just isn't enough information or  evidence yet the only thing I can  confirm is Winterfell is about to take a  serious beating I just hope that as long  as there is a stark in Winterfell they  can overcome whatever attack this may be  I think we are going to need to see John  ride Ragle as soon as possible if they  want a chance at stopping the night king  and his massive army John and Daenerys  will need to throw everything they have  at the night King and even that might  not be enough but only time will tell  I have made a few different videos where  I discuss how I think the Great War will  end but anything is possible at this  point  another photo was recently posted online  and it showed a handful of characters  arriving in Iceland which is very  interesting as well if you look at this  photo you can see tormund Brienne Jorah  Samwell Tarly and ginjury is right  beside Sam but he's kind of hard to see  John and Daenerys arrived in Iceland as  well and these photos do confirm two  things  Gendry will be back in torment is still  alive but what makes this even more  interesting is the fact that they're in  Iceland they typically only film here  when they are shooting scenes beyond the  wall but now that the wall was down in  the night King is south why would they  need to go back up there could there be  something beyond the wall that they need  to find or could they force the night  king in his army back up north like the  last hero did or  is the winter so severe now they have to  film in Iceland to depict a long night  type winter the night king typically  brings the storm with him so I am  thinking we could see Winterfell like  we've never seen it before if you  remember old main story then you should  know when the long night falls upon the  world things can get very intense snow  falls over a hundred feet deep people  freeze in their castles and people  starve and so on and so forth  whatever they are doing in Iceland has  me intrigued but I have a feeling most  of these scenes they are filming there  we'll just be in the north and not  beyond the wall because winter is here  and most of the north should look like  the landscapes in Iceland I don't want  to do a whole lot of crazy speculating  though because there just isn't enough  information right now but I told you I  would keep you up to  with whatever is going on so let me know  what you think down below do you have  any fun theories for why Winterfell is  burning and what does this mean for the  Starks I'm curious to see what you think  thanks for stopping by for this quick  update video I appreciate everyone for  watching and I also want to thank my  patreon supporters have a great night  everyone I'll see you soon but  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]

